     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">4.4. In 2021, the beta version of the &#x201c;Digital Technologies Radar for Disaster Risk Management&#x201d; has been co-developed by CB/ DRT and UNDP SDG AI Lab to effectively support UNDP and other development stakeholders in navigating digital solutions for disaster management. The DRM Digital Technologies Radar will allow for the monitoring and tracking of existing and emerging digital solutions. This would enable improved understanding of the technological landscape among development stakeholders and encourage adoption of proven solutions, while furthering UNDP as a thought leader on the use of innovative technologies in disaster contexts. The full version will be released in Q1 2022.
4.5. GARD workshops to train airport staff on preparedness were held in hybrid format using VR glasses and a team of trainers deployed in-country and remotely in Jamaica, Puerto Rico and Peru. The GARD global partnership has expanded to include Airports Council International in 2021, and is expecting ICAO and WFP affiliation in 2020. A new GARD programme concept has been developed by partners to be rolled out as of 2022, including a pilot regional programme for the Caribbean.
4.6. UNDP&#x2019;s Early Warning and Preparedness Policy Brief (draft) and the UNDP Service Offer on Disaster Early Warning and Preparedness are GPN products co-created by CB and BPPS. They provide a first-event comprehensive mapping of UNDP&#x2019;s programmatic areas as they related to preparedness and early warning across various thematic areas (including disaster and climate change), as well as a snapshot of UNDP&#x2019;s internal early warning and crisis preparedness resources geared towards UNDP Country Offices.</narrative>
